      en: "Estádio Nacional da Tundavala is a remarkable feature of the geography and culture of Angola. Located in Lubango, this 20,000-seat stadium is known for its unique architectural integration into the surrounding mountainous landscape. 20,000 seats. Built for Africa Cup. Near Tundavala gap. This landmark is part of the cultural heritage of Angola. Like many notable places in Angola, it combines regional character with wider significance. Thus, this place contributes to the diverse profile of Angola."
